    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or shows increasing negativity, as price tends to correct downward.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp upward spikes (e.g., >10% above recent peak) by applying a dampening factor to prevent overcorrection.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above or below 30-day moving average, adjust toward historical mean for 15-day window.",
    "For horizon 30d, reduce forecast magnitude if recent 5-day price decline exceeds 5% — indicates potential reversal.",
    "If sentiment history shows a recent shift from neutral to positive (e.g., 0.00 → 0.50), slightly increase forecast but cap at 10% above prior peak to avoid overestimation.",
    "When sentiment is consistently 0.00, assume no strong directional bias — use historical volatility-weighted average as baseline for correction."
